Split sum-type AST nodes into per-variant nodes

Each variant of Decl, Term, TypeExpr, PredExpr, FuncExpr, IfAtom,
ThenAtom and Stmt now lives in the arena under its own typed id
(VarTermId, EqualAtomId, ...). The sum-type enum itself is also
materialized as an arena node, so `ast.term(id)` and friends are just
the regular accessors generated by the accessor! macro instead of
hand-written dispatch functions.

Equal and Pred atoms are shared between IfAtom and ThenAtom: EqualAtomId
and PredAtomId can appear under either, with the enclosing IfAtom or
ThenAtom node recording which.
